{"step_index":171,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T21:54:27Z","model":"gemini-4-argon-high","input_tokens":3090,"cache_read_tokens":132062,"output_tokens":1204,"content":"The Python `html.escape` program has been formalized in Lean 4 at [20_html_escape.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/20_html_escape.lean).\n\n### Summary of Formalization (`«20_html_escape»`)\n\n1. **Functional Implementation** ([20_html_escape.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/20_html_escape.lean#L21-L70)):\n   - `pre_escape`, `replaceChar`, `escape`, `benchmark_escape`, `escapeChar`, `isSpecialChar`, and `check`.\n   - `escape` mirrors Python's sequential replacement order (`&` $\\to$ `<` $\\to$ `>`, and when `quote = true`, `\"` $\\to$ `'`).\n\n2. **Unit Tests & Pre-condition** ([20_html_escape.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/20_html_escape.lean#L72-L103)):\n   - Ground tests via `example : ... := by native_decide` and `#eval` covering `quote = true`, `quote = false`, order sensitivity (`\"&<\"` and `\"&lt;\"`), and `check`.\n   - `Pre (s : String) (quote : Bool := true) : Prop`.\n\n3. **Properties, Theorems & Post-Condition** ([20_html_escape.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/20_html_escape.lean#L105-L645)):\n   - `single_pass_prop` / `single_pass_thm`: Sequential replacement of `&`, `<`, `>`, `\"`, `'` equals single-pass character-wise escaping `escapeChar` (no double-escaping).\n   - `empty_prop` / `empty_thm`: `escape \"\" quote = \"\"`.\n   - `append_prop` / `append_thm`: `escape (s₁ ++ s₂) quote = escape s₁ quote ++ escape s₂ quote`.\n   - `special_chars_prop` / `special_chars_thm`: Exact entity translation of `&`, `<`, `>`, `\"`, `'` under both `quote = true` and `quote = false`.\n   - `no_angle_brackets_prop` / `no_angle_brackets_thm`: `'<'` and `'>'` never appear in `escape s quote`.\n   - `no_quotes_when_quote_true_prop` / `no_quotes_when_quote_true_thm`: `'\"'` and `'\\''` never appear in `escape s true`.\n   - `quotes_preserved_when_quote_false_prop` / `quotes_preserved_when_quote_false_thm`: Counts of `'\"'` and `'\\''` are preserved when `quote = false`.\n   - `exact_length_prop` / `exact_length_thm`: Exact output length formula in terms of input length and counts of special characters.\n   - `length_bounds_prop` / `length_bounds_thm`: `s.length ≤ (escape s quote).length ≤ (if quote then 6 else 5) * s.length`.\n   - `unchanged_iff_no_special_prop` / `unchanged_iff_no_special_thm`: `escape s quote = s ↔ ∀ c ∈ s.data, isSpecialChar c quote = false`.\n   - `ampersand_count_prop` / `ampersand_count_thm` & `semicolon_count_prop` / `semicolon_count_thm`: Exact counts of `'&'` and `';'` in the output.\n   - `quote_flag_relation_prop` / `quote_flag_relation_thm`: Relationship between `escape s true` and `escape s false`.\n   - `injective_prop` / `injective_thm`: `escape s₁ quote = escape s₂ quote ↔ s₁ = s₂`.\n   - `benchmark_escape_eq_prop` / `benchmark_escape_eq_thm`: `benchmark_escape s quote = escape s quote`.\n   - `Post_prop` & `escape_correct` ([20_html_escape.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/20_html_escape.lean#L618-L686)): Conjunction of all properties, randomized Plausible PBTs and bounded `native_decide` PBTs for every `_prop` and `Post_prop`, and full correctness proof `Pre s quote → Post_prop s quote`.\n\n4. **Imperative Implementations & Equivalence Proofs** ([20_html_escape.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/20_html_escape.lean#L688-L804)):\n   - `replaceCharImp`, `escapeImp` (multi-pass mutable state), and `escapeSinglePassImp` (single-pass mutable buffer) using `Id.run do`.\n   - Full equivalence theorems `replaceChar_eq_replaceCharImp`, `escape_eq_escapeImp`, `escape_eq_escapeSinglePassImp`, and `escapeImp_eq_escapeSinglePassImp`."}
